  <template id="tmpl-finalthesis">
    <div class="modal-head">
      <span class="modal-cat mono">film &amp; thesis</span>
      <h2>Final Thesis</h2>
      <span class="modal-tag mono">vimeo / 945507158</span>
    </div>
    <div class="scan-frame">
      <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner tr"></span><span class="corner bl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
      <div class="scan-label mono">SCAN_05 · FINAL THESIS</div>
      <div class="video-embed">
        <iframe src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/945507158?title=0&amp;byline=0&amp;portrait=0&amp;badge=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" title="Final Thesis" loading="lazy"></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="work-desc">An exploration of feelings presented as a short film — a specific aesthetic applied to computer-generated clips to talk about the hard-to-describe fragility of human connection. The intention is to challenge the audience through non-linear, experimental narratives that blur reality and perception. Each of us sees the world slightly differently; this film celebrates that divergence, and asks what it is that forms our identity.</p>
  </template>

  <template id="tmpl-visualjam">
    <div class="modal-head">
      <span class="modal-cat mono">film &amp; thesis</span>
      <h2>Final Visual Jam</h2>
      <span class="modal-tag mono">vimeo / 1052961100</span>
    </div>
    <div class="scan-frame">
      <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner tr"></span><span class="corner bl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
      <div class="scan-label mono">SCAN_06 · FINAL VISUAL JAM</div>
      <div class="video-embed">
        <iframe src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1052961100?title=0&amp;byline=0&amp;portrait=0&amp;badge=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" title="Final Visual Jam" loading="lazy"></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="work-desc">A study of entanglement in the context of a long-distance relationship — focused on the lack of physical closeness, and the toll that takes. The piece uses quantum entanglement as a metaphor to fuel connection across distance: the music is a translation of quantum data into instruments and notes, with noisy qubits introducing random instrumentation that drifts in and out of the beat.</p>
  </template>


